  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 73ff519377b990a4c81cd1461a3c1f62, type: 3}
  m_Name: Tala_W41_Teach
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::DialogueNode
  speakerName: Tala
  speakerPortrait: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 0c019a51009268f43a5d4f67570f27cb, type: 3}
  dialogueText: 'Padayawantayo pay ti panagbilang.


    Iti Ilokano, ti ''uppat''
    ket kayatna a saoen ti ''four.''


    Mabalinmo nga agusar iti daytoy no agbilangka
    iti uppat a banag, kas iti uppat a piraso ti bagnet.


    Denggem a naimbag:
    uppat.


    Ita, padasem nga ibagam ti ''uppat'' iti bukodmo a timek.'
  translatedText: 'Let''s keep counting.

    In Ilokano, ''uppat'' means ''four.''

    You
    can use it when counting four objects, such as four pieces of Bagnet.

    Now,
    try saying ''uppat'' yourself.'
